Ragged Roost is an abandoned mining town a little under a day's drive out of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], barely on modern maps. Its mine was small, and once ore could be shipped in from the [[Phenomena/Infinite Horizon|Infinite Horizon]] for less than it cost to dig here, there was no reason to keep working it, so the Orgs took what was worth packing and left the rest. A rusted sign at the town line reads "Welcome to Ragged Roost, population" with the number scribbled out to zero. A main street runs through the town with a few streets branching off it, one and two story buildings, and above the town on the mountainside sits the old rock crusher and its conveyor, unused.

The town is the site of the [[Phenomena/Pilgrimage|pilgrimage]]. For the gathering the old oil street lamps have been given electricity and hung with fairy lights, with banners reading "Pilgrimage Welcome" hanging from them, and tables of hors d'oeuvres and champagne line the main street. Hundreds of guests walk the street in elegant dress and masks, animal masks and plain ones and ornate masquerade masks, some of them with three or four armed attendants. Spotlights throw light into the sky, bright enough to be seen ten miles off. Signs direct cars to a parking lot at the edge of town, where guests have their invitations checked at a table and are handed masks.

At the middle of town stands the completed Istrian strider, a platform carried on eight legs with buildings set on top, three or four stories up and the size of a cruise ship. Its name is the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]. The pilgrimage's host has set its guests to hunting the twenty [[Phenomena/Keystone|keystones]].

Crossing the town line brings a pins-and-needles feeling at the small of the back, and every raiment within the town turns a plain matte gray, all of them the same color, shape and size and half-transparent, so that no guest can be read for their god. The blessings themselves still work. [[Aut]]'s mark still shows on [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] when he calls it up, and still answers him.

Beyond the main street, a path marked with crossed swords leads to a disused train yard where Harlequins run a trial by combat, and one marked with a fairy ring leads off toward the town's outskirts.
